build/
*.dsk
*.mgt
!reference/**/*.dsk
!reference/**/*.mgt
*.bin
!reference/**/*.bin
!tools/editor-prototype/fonts/*.bin
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
.worktrees/
# In-tree Go build binaries. `go build` inside a tools/<pkg> package drops a
# binary named after its directory alongside the source, where it's easy to
# `git add` by accident. One precise entry per main-package output path (no
# blanket tools/** that could mask real source). The produced binary is
# <dir>/<dirname>; aarch64dec's main lives under cmd/, so it has both the
# parent-dir build form and the in-cmd-dir build form.
tools/aarch64dec/aarch64dec
tools/aarch64dec/cmd/aarch64dec/aarch64dec
tools/build-disk/build-disk
tools/tables-gen/tables-gen
tools/comment-bench/comment-bench
tools/z80-test-harness-go/z80-test-harness-go
tools/i62-bdos-experiment/build-i62-disk/build-i62-disk
tools/font-proof/font-proof
tools/registry/registry

# Transient advisory lock the registry CLI flocks to serialize concurrent
# mutations (tools/registry/lock.go); runtime-only, never committed.
registry/.lock

# sam-aarch64's default .tbn output beside a vendored source (release.s is
# tracked; its compiled .tbn is a derived artifact — the canonical gate scripts
# write .tbn to build/, never here).
tests/release/release.s.tbn


# --- Override global ~/.gitignore_global for this (personal) repo ---
# The global excludesfile ignores the whole .claude/ directory + superpowers
# (a guard so work repos never commit Claude files — company policy). This is
# a personal repo, so we surgically re-include the version-controlled session
# handover hook config, while keeping the agent worktrees (and everything else
# under .claude/) ignored. NOTE: a parent dir must be un-ignored before a file
# inside it can be re-included, hence the !.claude/ then .claude/* dance.
!.claude/
.claude/*
!.claude/settings.json
# Project skills are version-controlled (shared with every agent in the repo);
# re-include the skills tree (the dir, then its contents — the un-ignore dance).
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/skills/**
.claude/worktrees/

# i62 experiment artifacts: Atom Lite hard-disk images are generated
# locally by tools/i62-bdos-experiment/make-atomlite-hdf.py (and normally
# land in build/); never commit one.
*.hdf

# The bootblock flasher (eeprom_flash_chunk1.asm) embeds the trinity-autoboot
# bootloader (Colin Piggot's boot block + our patches) as DEFB data. That
# bootloader is a private artifact kept out of the repo and CI (q55); the data
# file is regenerated locally from the sibling repo via `make gen-bootloader-data`.
src/netboot/bootloader_chunk1_data.asm
